FatFs in ReactOS
================

This directory contains FatFs R0.16 with the upstream patch 2 applied.
It is the common FAT/exFAT implementation used by the image host tool,
FreeLdr, and the exFAT filesystem driver. Each consumer supplies only the
FatFs media-access and allocation callbacks appropriate to its environment.

Upstream: https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/
Archive:  https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/arc/ff16.zip
Archive SHA-256: 99f7dc1f7e095356e4a9e3dbe29959090d8b948afe2bbc5441e52fdf4b85449e
Release: R0.16, July 22, 2025

Applied upstream patches, in order:

1. https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/patch/ff16p1.diff
   SHA-256: 7996ddc3135f3d534a8153f7d75d587030e5c8551b003c3b7ee823ffb7fc64bf
2. https://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/patch/ff16p2.diff
   SHA-256: 5cd39f1fc299f0f1dec9fa1ce544dc0bc048b2f6eb3b8161476ed20f9cf1e290

ReactOS changes are intentionally limited to:

* ffconf.h enables exFAT, UTF-8 long names, formatting, 64-bit LBA, and
  the media geometry needed by all three consumers. FF_LFN_UNICODE remains
  overridable so the kernel exFAT driver can use UTF-16 without a second copy
  of the configuration file.
* ff.h accepts FF_USE_REACTOS_TYPES so target builds use the SDK's fixed-width
  Windows types without including the user-mode Windows umbrella header.
* CMakeLists.txt defines the target-side static library.
* ff.c provides ReactOS-only replacements for selected exFAT optimizations
  identified in "Patent-related changes" below.

Patent-related changes
----------------------

The __REACTOS__ branches replace selected upstream NameHash and NoFatChain
optimization bodies. Where upstream contains an implementation, the #else
branch contains only a patent and expiration-date placeholder.

1. Directory lookup by NameHash: US8321439B2 (adjusted expiration date
   2027-03-09) and US10614032B2 (adjusted expiration date 2028-01-27).
   dir_find() compares candidate name lengths and characters without using
   the on-disk NameHash as a pre-filter.

2. NoFatChain state and flag handling: US8725772B2 (anticipated expiration
   date 2027-05-23). remove_chain(), f_mkdir(), and f_expand() keep locally
   modified chains on the FAT instead of marking them contiguous.

3. NoFatChain extension: US9122695B2 and US9558223B2 (anticipated expiration
   date 2027-05-23), and US7873596B2 (adjusted expiration date 2028-03-27).
   create_chain() records new and extended chains in the FAT.

These dates and statuses were checked in Google Patents on 2026-07-24.
Google's status data is an estimate, not a legal conclusion. Recheck the
USPTO file history before replacing any placeholder.

The kernel driver and FreeLoader do not select data I/O paths from exFAT
allocation flags or construct file extents. File data is accessed through
FatFs.

The media-access implementation is not kept in this directory. This preserves
the upstream separation between the filesystem core and platform I/O.
